  "items": [
    {
      "id": "at://did:plc:flxq4uyjfotciovpw3x3fxnu/app.bsky.feed.post/3n333h3yyoc2g",
      "handle": "emollick.bsky.social",
      "display_name": "Ethan Mollick",
      "text": "Thing I am hearing from a number of big firms, from manufacturers to financial services: we have scattered teams of 2-3 people using AI that are doing the work of dozens of folks in a fraction of the time, creating large-scale management fights over the implications and politics for the organization",
      "url": "https://bsky.app/profile/emollick.bsky.social/post/3n333h3yyoc2g",
      "posted_at": "2026-11-24T16:39:19.909Z",
      "likes": 183,
      "replies": 13,
      "reposts": 12,
      "score": 7.4,
      "score_parts": {
        "engagement": 2.3,
        "recency": 0.9,
        "age_hours": 13.9
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "at://did:plc:flxq4uyjfotciovpw3x3fxnu/app.bsky.feed.post/3n2zykguajs2g",
      "handle": "emollick.bsky.social",
      "display_name": "Ethan Mollick",
      "text": "Two kinds of people: those watching the AI agent swarm trying to crack P=NP and those watching the AI agent swarm trying to (illegally) port the Xbox version of GTA 6 to the PC.\n\nHere is the P=NP one: pequalnp.com",
      "url": "https://bsky.app/profile/emollick.bsky.social/post/3n2zykguajs2g",
      "posted_at": "2026-11-24T06:14:50.987Z",
      "likes": 183,
      "replies": 8,
      "reposts": 26,
      "score": 7.3,
      "score_parts": {
        "engagement": 2.4,
        "recency": 0.9,
        "age_hours": 24.3
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "at://did:plc:flxq4uyjfotciovpw3x3fxnu/app.bsky.feed.post/3n2xc6e3yec2m",
      "handle": "emollick.bsky.social",
      "display_name": "Ethan Mollick",
      "text": "Not that AI discourse has ever been great, but \"of course LLMs are good at math\" both misses that \"good at math\" is an *slight* understatement in the context of solving the Reimann Hypothesis & also ignores the fact that LLMs were not actually \"good at math\" until very recent breakthroughs.",
      "url": "https://bsky.app/profile/emollick.bsky.social/post/3n2xc6e3yec2m",
      "posted_at": "2026-11-23T04:29:03.646Z",
      "likes": 281,
      "replies": 11,
      "reposts": 21,
      "score": 7.1,
      "score_parts": {
        "engagement": 2.5,
        "recency": 0.7,
        "age_hours": 50.1
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "at://did:plc:ppxzeec7mddu2zh57wjqzquy/app.bsky.feed.post/3n2zb3ilxpk2m",
      "handle": "markriedl.bsky.social",
      "display_name": "Mark Riedl",
      "text": "Anthropic just dropped VP ≠ VNP. If it holds up this means there aren't polynomial-size circuits for permanent over the reals using addition and multiplication gates and arbitrary constants. This doesn't settle P v NP.",
      "url": "https://bsky.app/profile/markriedl.bsky.social/post/3n2zb3ilxpk2m",
      "posted_at": "2026-11-23T23:14:52.000Z",
      "likes": 34,
      "replies": 3,
      "reposts": 11,
      "score": 5.9,
      "score_parts": {
        "engagement": 1.7,
        "recency": 0.8,
        "age_hours": 31.3
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "at://did:plc:rrjvo5jwuateqep2i7ih5ckl/app.bsky.feed.post/3n2yruspowk2r",
      "handle": "cfiesler.bsky.social",
      "display_name": "Casey Fiesler",
      "text": "A likely explanation is that students with very similar responses used an LLM to assist with this assignment. So the reason I am pointing this out is that I hope it will be a useful lesson to you on the limitations of LLMs - particularly what we learned in class about homogenization.",
      "url": "https://bsky.app/profile/cfiesler.bsky.social/post/3n2yruspowk2r",
      "posted_at": "2026-11-23T18:42:43.034Z",
      "likes": 28,
      "replies": 1,
      "reposts": 2,
      "score": 5.4,
      "score_parts": {
        "engagement": 1.5,
        "recency": 0.8,
        "age_hours": 35.8
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "at://did:plc:rrjvo5jwuateqep2i7ih5ckl/app.bsky.feed.post/3n2ysbebic22r",
      "handle": "cfiesler.bsky.social",
      "display_name": "Casey Fiesler",
      "text": "Additionally, in this course you are permitted to use AI as long as you disclose. So if this was the case for you, it is worth considering why you decided not to do so. When you do not want others to know you use AI, you could potentially learn something from some self reflection about why that is.",
      "url": "https://bsky.app/profile/cfiesler.bsky.social/post/3n2ysbebic22r",
      "posted_at": "2026-11-23T18:49:44.097Z",
      "likes": 24,
      "replies": 1,
      "reposts": 1,
      "score": 5.3,
      "score_parts": {
        "engagement": 1.4,
        "recency": 0.8,
        "age_hours": 35.7
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "at://did:plc:rrjvo5jwuateqep2i7ih5ckl/app.bsky.feed.post/3n2yryorh5s2r",
      "handle": "cfiesler.bsky.social",
      "display_name": "Casey Fiesler",
      "text": "And of course when we take this issue at the scale of society, frequent uses of AI in this way and subsequent impacts on human creativity could have a broad harmful homogenizing impact.",
      "url": "https://bsky.app/profile/cfiesler.bsky.social/post/3n2yryorh5s2r",
      "posted_at": "2026-11-23T18:44:53.116Z",
      "likes": 21,
      "replies": 1,
      "reposts": 2,
      "score": 5.2,
      "score_parts": {
        "engagement": 1.4,
        "recency": 0.8,
        "age_hours": 35.8
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "at://did:plc:3igkkqe5nkm66olc4y2syzpy/app.bsky.feed.post/3n32vb2ci3c2i",
      "handle": "markriedl.bsky.social",
      "display_name": "Mark Riedl",
      "text": "Be nice, Micah. These people make very convincing statements, bolstered by an irresponsible media. As the Rationalist cult breaks containment, it will take time to inform people who are not keeping an eye on these weirdos. Not even everyone who studies AI is aware of the dangerous undercurrents.",
      "url": "https://bsky.app/profile/markriedl.bsky.social/post/3n32vb2ci3c2i",
      "posted_at": "2026-11-24T14:48:34.345Z",
      "likes": 0,
      "replies": 2,
      "reposts": 0,
      "score": 4.1,
      "score_parts": {
